# AGENT.md — src/infrastructure/

The outer persistence layer. Implements the repository interfaces (ports)
defined in the domain layer.

## What lives here

- `persistence/<module>.repository.ts` — in-memory implementation (when no ORM is selected).
- `persistence/<module>.prisma.repository.ts` — Prisma adapter.
- `persistence/<module>.orm-entity.ts` — TypeORM entity class (with `@Entity()`).
- `persistence/<module>.typeorm.repository.ts` — TypeORM adapter.
- `persistence/<module>.schema.ts` — Mongoose schema.
- `persistence/<module>.mongoose.repository.ts` — Mongoose adapter.

## Rules

1. **Implements domain interfaces.** Every repository class here
   `implements I<PascalCase>Repository` from `src/domain/repositories/`.
2. Domain entities are mapped to/from persistence models manually via
   `toDomain()` / constructor calls. No ORM-entity-as-domain-entity shortcuts.
3. Only one database client is created (in `src/shared/database/`).
   Repositories import the shared instance — never create their own connection.
4. Mongoose repositories use `.lean()` and explicitly type the result
   before mapping to domain entities.
